    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-19T11:37:46+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-19T11:37:46+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T01:07:46Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T01:07:46Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system and associated trough over Western Australia move across the state during Thursday, clearing to the east early Friday. A high pressure system will then move across southern SA from Friday, before a trough and cold front move across the west late Saturday and across the rest of SA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW002" description="Yorke Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <warning-summary type="fire_weather_warning" start-time-local="2026-11-19T05:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T18:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">Fire Weather Warning for the Yorke Peninsula fire weather district for Thursday</warning-summary>
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the late afternoon and evening. A thunderstorm likely. Winds northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h turning north to northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon and evening. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low to mid 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Extreme</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Slight chance of a shower in the early morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the early morning. Mostly sunny day. Winds northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h turning west to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the late morning and early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the south in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the south in the evening. Winds northwest to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then becoming northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching 28 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">High chance of showers, most likely in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning. Mostly sunny afternoon. Winds northerly 20 to 30 km/h shifting west to southwesterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
